            <ArticleTitle>Oesophageal duplication cyst: an unusual cause of retrosternal pain and dysphagia in an adult.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e242-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Oesophageal duplication cysts in adults are a rare entity and are mostly asymptomatic. We describe the imaging findings in a rare case of oesophageal duplication cyst simulating cold abscess, causing retrosternal pain and dysphagia in a 25-year-old man.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
